{
  "_schema": "A recipe runs on a timer while a building of `building` stands and every `input` is in stock; each cycle scales with how many of that building stand. Extraction recipes use `input_resource` (a deposit node type) instead of `input`: a drill within 1 cell of that deposit yields the full `output`, any other drill yields `output × trace_factor` (the ore is thin in bulk regolith everywhere). `stop_at` pauses the recipe once an output reaches that stock level, so the fabricator maintains stocks instead of draining one input into one part.",

  "drill_regolith": {
    "display_name": "Drill Regolith",
    "input": {},
